# Hugo templates. Not a temporary exclusion: no safe formatter exists.
#
# Prettier's built-in html parser does not understand Go template actions at
# all. prettier-plugin-go-template (v0.0.15) parses them but treats whitespace
# around {{ ... }} as insignificant, which silently corrupts output. Verified
# against a before/after `hugo --minify` build of this site:
#
#   class="tab-button{{ if eq $first . }} selected{{ end }}"
#     -> class="tab-button{{ if eq $first . }}selected{{ end }}"
#     -> renders as class="tab-buttonselected", losing the CSS class
#
#   {{- if $u.IsAbs }} rel="external" ...
#     -> renders as <a href="..."rel="external">, malformed HTML
#
# Whitespace is part of the output in Hugo templates, especially with {{- -}}
# trim markers, so reformatting them is not safe. The CI build is what
# validates these instead: a broken template fails `hugo`.
layouts

